# Frontend build-time configuration for a production deployment of
# Zaphira PPC Control (Vite bakes VITE_* vars into the build at build
# time -- this is never a secret, just an address).
#
# Copy this file to .env.production (or set the same variable as a
# build-time environment variable in whatever platform builds/hosts the
# frontend — Railway, Vercel, Netlify, etc.) and point it at your deployed
# Amazon Ads backend's own HTTPS URL (see server/README.md's "Production
# deployment (Railway)" section for deploying that backend).
#
# Never put a Client Secret, refresh token, or access token in this file
# or in any VITE_*/frontend environment variable — those live ONLY in the
# backend's own server-side environment variables (see
# server/.env.amazon.local.example), never in anything bundled into the
# browser.

VITE_AMAZON_BACKEND_URL=https://<your-railway-backend-service>.up.railway.app
